{"id":"70f89005-eb75-43f4-88e9-95822343fe83","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.07.045","title":"Multimodal brain cell atlas across the adult macaque lifespan","title_zh":"跨成年猕猴寿命的多模态脑细胞图谱","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.07.045","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.07.045","abstract":"High-throughput single-cell omics of non-human primate brain tissue provides a powerful platform to investigate the molecular basis of brain aging. Here, we present a comprehensive transcriptomic and chromatin accessibility atlas of 2,955,873 nuclei from eight brain regions of 23 female cynomolgus macaques spanning the adult lifespan, including exceptionally old individuals. Our analyses reveal dynamic, cell-subtype- and region-specific age-related changes in core brain functions, including synaptic communication and axon myelination. We identify multicellular networks in the pons and medulla as a previously unrecognized hotspot of primate brain aging, highlighting white matter vulnerability as a central feature of aging. Integration with human brain aging and neurodegeneration datasets reveals both shared and divergent molecular mechanisms. We further define transcription factors and age-related chromatin remodeling programs linked to longevity and neurodegeneration. This spatiotemporal atlas establishes a foundational framework for understanding the cellular and regulatory architecture of primate brain aging and its links to disease.","abstract_zh":"高通量单细胞组学对非人灵长类脑组织的研究为探究脑衰老的分子基础提供了强大平台。本文呈现了来自23只成年雌性长尾猕猴（覆盖成年寿命，包括极老个体）八个脑区的2955873个细胞核的全转录组和染色质可及性全景图谱。我们的分析揭示了核心脑功能（如突触通讯和轴突髓鞘化）在细胞亚型和脑区层面随年龄变化的动态特征。我们在延髓和脑干发现了多细胞网络，表明这是灵长类脑衰老的前所未识别的热点，突显白质脆弱性是衰老的核心特征。与人类脑衰老和神经退行性疾病数据集的整合显示了共享与差异的分子机制。我们进一步定义了与寿命和神经退行性疾病相关的转录因子及年龄相关染色质重塑程序。该时空图谱为理解灵长类脑衰老的细胞与调控结构及其与疾病的关联奠定了基础框架。","snippet":"High-throughput single-cell omics of non-human primate brain tissue provides a powerful platform to investigate the molecular basis of brain aging. Here, we present a comprehensive transcriptomic and chromatin accessibility atlas of 2,955,873 nuclei from eight brain regions of 23 female cynomolgus macaques spanning the adult lifespan, including exceptionally old individuals. Our analyses reveal dynamic, cell-subtype…","translated_at":"2026-08-29T17:38:52.226667Z","translation_model":"openai/gpt-oss-20b","source_category":"doi","article_type":"journal-article","volume":"189","issue":"22","published_at":"2026-08-18T00:00:00","acquired_at":"2026-08-18T16:58:25Z","display_date":"2026-08-18T16:58:25Z","display_date_source":"acquired","online_published_at":"2026-08-18T00:00:00","print_published_at":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","first_author":"Xiao Zhang","authors_text":"Xiao Zhang, Guangyao Lai, Xiangyu Guo, Wen Ma, Yue Yuan, Han Zhang, Bo Zhang, Peng Fan, Xingyuan Liu, Pengcheng Guo, Juan An, Jinxiu Li, Keke Huang, Xiaoyan Li, Jing Zuo, Liang Wu, Shuncheng Shangguan, Feng Yu, Yuchen Xiang, Yuebei Hu, Yuxuan Liu, Yunting Huang, Yiting Lin, Dajian He, Mingtian Pan, Laiqiang Chen, Bang Li, Jiawei Zhang, Qintian Guo, Weili Yang, Peng Yin, Shihua Li, Xiaolan Zhang, Tao Yang, Xiaofeng Wei, Yuan Lv, Baoming Qin, Xiaobing Qing, Qiuting Deng, Yaling Huang, Chang Liu, Lei Han, Shiping Liu, Dajiang Qin, Zhen Liu, Yi Zhou, Liang Qiao, Chengyu Li, Yanxiao Zhang, Zunpeng Liu, Yan Li, Paulina Carriba, Mara Dierssen, Giacomo Volpe, Simon Graf, Ian Ferenc Diks, Matthias Flotho, Rafal P. Krol, Jan Mulder, Chaiyaboot Ariyachet, Nattiya Hirankarn, Andrew P. Hutchins, Andreas Keller, Patrick H. Maxwell, David C. Rubinsztein, Pura Muñoz-Cánoves, Xiaolei Liu, Hung-Fat Tse, Muming Poo, Bo Wang, Longqi Liu, Ying Gu, Jun Xie, Xun Xu, Xiaojiang Li, Chuanyu Liu, Yiwei Lai, Miguel A. Esteban, Mingyuan Liu","authors":[{"position":0,"given_name":"Xiao","family_name":"Zhang","full_name":"Xiao Zhang","affiliation":null},{"position":1,"given_name":"Guangyao","family_name":"Lai","full_name":"Guangyao Lai","affiliation":null},{"position":2,"given_name":"Xiangyu","family_name":"Guo","full_name":"Xiangyu Guo","affiliati